    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm working on a lit review and i'm a bit stuck on citations. if i have a source with like 5 authors, how do i do the in-text citation for apa 7th vs chicago style? i keep getting them mixed up.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For APA 7th style, you should list the first author's last name followed by \"et al.\" when there are four or more authors. For example, (Smith et al., 2020). In the Chicago style, when there are five or more authors, you list only the first author's last name followed by \"et al.\" and the year, like this: Smith et al. (2020).\n\nRemember, the key difference lies in how you list the authors and their work in your in-text citations. Always check the latest style guide for specific rules and formatting.",
